<!--
  Office Deployment Tool configuration - Microsoft Visio for ENG 5105.
  Run as:  setup.exe /configure Visio-Config.xml

  ============================ READ BEFORE FIRST USE ============================
  THIS FILE IS A TEMPLATE WITH ONE UNVERIFIED FIELD: the Product ID below.
  Everything else is mechanical; the SKU is a licensing fact only UNIV can
  confirm. Get it wrong and setup.exe either fails outright or installs a Visio
  nobody can activate.

    VisioProRetail   - Visio Plan 2 assigned per user in Microsoft 365 (this is
                       what the guide's link describes, so it is the default here)
    VisioStdRetail   - Visio Plan 1 / Standard, subscription
    VisioProXVolume  - Visio LTSC Professional, KMS-activated volume licence
    VisioStdXVolume  - Visio LTSC Standard, KMS-activated volume licence

  Campus almost certainly has ONE of the two volume SKUs if Visio is licensed
  through the CSU agreement rather than per-student M365 assignment. Ask whoever
  owns the Microsoft 365 tenant, then change ProductID below and delete this
  paragraph.
  ================================================================================

  TWO THINGS THAT WILL BREAK THIS IF IGNORED

  1. CHANNEL AND ARCHITECTURE MUST MATCH THE OFFICE ALREADY ON THE IMAGE.
     Click-to-Run allows exactly one channel and one bitness per machine. If the
     image ships Microsoft 365 Apps on Current Channel x64 (the normal case) then
     this file must say Current and 64 - which it does. If the image is on
     Monthly Enterprise or Semi-Annual, change Channel to match, or setup.exe
     will refuse. Check with:
         "C:\Program Files\Common Files\microsoft shared\ClickToRun\OfficeC2RClient.exe"
     or read HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Office\ClickToRun\Configuration ->
     CDNBaseUrl / Platform / AudienceData.

  2. SHARED COMPUTER ACTIVATION IS NOT OPTIONAL ON A LAB LAPTOP.
     SharedComputerLicensing=1 below is what lets many different students sign in
     to the same machine and each use their own Visio licence. Without it the
     FIRST student to open Visio consumes one of their five device activations
     and every later student is locked out. This setting only applies to the
     subscription SKUs; it is harmless (ignored) on the volume ones.

  WHAT THIS FILE DELIBERATELY DOES NOT DO
     It does not list Microsoft 365 Apps / Office in <Add>, and it has no
     <Remove> block. Listing only Visio ADDS Visio to whatever Click-to-Run
     installation already exists and leaves Word/Excel/Outlook untouched. Adding
     an Office product here would re-stage several GB and could change the
     image's channel underneath the rest of the fleet.

  OFFLINE VS ONLINE: with no local payload, setup.exe streams it from
  Microsoft's CDN (~1-4 GB). To make it offline, run
      setup.exe /download Visio-Config.xml
  once on the bench FROM INSIDE this folder - that creates an Office\ subfolder
  next to setup.exe. LEAVE SourcePath OUT of this file: in /configure mode with
  SourcePath omitted, the ODT looks for that Office\ folder next to setup.exe
  first and falls back to the CDN only when it is absent. That beats hardcoding
  a path (stick drive letters vary) and beats a {source} placeholder (nothing
  expands placeholders inside this XML - only the card's install.arguments).
  Given that campus HTTPS interception already broke winget on this fleet (see
  the PuTTY card), pre-downloading is the safer path for a 30-laptop cart.
-->
<Configuration ID="labdeploy-vep5105-visio">

  <Add OfficeClientEdition="64" Channel="Current">
    <Product ID="VisioProRetail">
      <Language ID="en-us" />
      <!-- Nothing to exclude: Visio is a single app. -->
    </Product>
  </Add>

  <!-- No user interface, no EULA prompt, no reboot: this runs unattended
       inside LabDeploy's install queue. -->
  <Display Level="None" AcceptEULA="TRUE" />
  <Property Name="AUTOACTIVATE" Value="0" />
  <Property Name="FORCEAPPSHUTDOWN" Value="TRUE" />
  <Property Name="SharedComputerLicensing" Value="1" />
  <Property Name="DeviceBasedLicensing" Value="0" />

  <!-- Keep Office updating the way the rest of the image does; do not let this
       one product pin the machine to a different servicing cadence. -->
  <Updates Enabled="TRUE" Channel="Current" />

  <!-- setup.exe writes its own log here; LabDeploy's log points at it when the
       install fails, which is the only way to tell a licensing refusal apart
       from a download failure. -->
  <Logging Level="Standard" Path="%TEMP%\LabDeploy-Visio" />

  <!-- No RemoveMSI: these are freshly imaged machines with no legacy MSI Office.
       If that ever changes, add <RemoveMSI /> here rather than uninstalling by
       hand. -->

</Configuration>
